---@field value? string The value of the field that caused the error.
---@field location? paypal.invoicing_v2.ErrorLocation
---@field issue string The unique, fine-grained application-level error code.
---@field description? string The human-readable description for an issue. The description can change over the lifetime of an API, so clients must not depend on this value.

---The request-related [HATEOAS link](/api/rest/responses/#hateoas-links) information.
---@class paypal.invoicing_v2.ErrorLinkDescription
---@field href string The complete target URL. To make the related call, combine the method with this [URI Template-formatted](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc6570) link. For pre-processing, include the `$`, `(`, and `)` characters. The `href` is the key HATEOAS component that links a completed call with a subsequent call.
---@field rel string The [link relation type](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc5988#section-4), which serves as an ID for a link that unambiguously describes the semantics of the link. See [Link Relations](https://www.iana.org/assignments/link-relations/link-relations.xhtml).
---@field method? paypal.invoicing_v2.ErrorLinkDescriptionMethod The HTTP method required to make the related call.

