---@field note? string A note to the invoice recipient. Also appears on the invoice notification email.
---@field terms_and_conditions? string The general terms of the invoice. Can include return or cancellation policy and other terms and conditions.
---@field memo? string A private bookkeeping memo for the user.
---@field attachments? paypal.invoicing_v2.FileReferenceList
---@field invoice_number? string The invoice number. Default is the number that is auto-incremented number from the last number.
---@field invoice_date? string The invoice date as specificed by the sender, in [Internet date and time format](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc3339#section-5.6). Only UTC is supported in response. For example, *yyyy*-*MM*-*dd*T*z*.
---@field payment_term? paypal.invoicing_v2.InvoicePaymentTerm The payment due date for the invoice. Value is either but not both <code>term_type</code> or <code>due_date</code>.
---@field metadata? paypal.invoicing_v2.Metadata The audit metadata. Captures all invoicing actions on create, send, update, and cancel.

